---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ArrowIcon from '../components/ArrowIcon.astro';
import Rocket from '../components/Rocket.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---

<Base title="About | Vansh" ogImagePath="og/about.png" ogImageAlt="About Vansh">
  <section class="shell page-section about-page">
    <div class="eyebrow">
      <span class="status-dot"></span>
      <span>DOSSIER // BEHIND THE NOTEBOOK</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="page-title">
      Hi, I’m Vansh<span class="accent">.</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="about-lead">
      A mechanical engineering student concentrating in aerospace at Hofstra University,
      tinkerer with manufacturing tooling, and daily Fedora Linux user who enjoys understanding
      governing physical models and building reliable systems.
    </p>

    <div class="about-columns">
      <div class="prose about-prose">
        <h2>Engineering, with curiosity.</h2>

        <p>
          I’m a mechanical engineering student at Hofstra University,
          concentrating in aerospace and graduating in 2027. I also serve
          as co-president of our AIAA chapter, helping create opportunities
          for students to explore aerospace through projects, workshops,
          and connections beyond the classroom.
        </p>

        <p>
          Aircraft design, rocketry, and numerical simulation are particular interests
          of mine. I’m drawn to the process of taking a question, working
          through the physics, and developing something that can be modeled,
          built, or tested.
        </p>

        <h2>From drawings to the shop floor.</h2>

        <p>
          I spent six months as an Aerospace Manufacturing Engineer Co-op
          at Arkwin Industries, working with aerospace hydraulic actuators
          and the tooling and processes used to manufacture them.
          My work included inspection fixtures, CNC workholding, custom
          cutting tools, engineering drawings, and manufacturing documentation.
        </p>

        <p>
          That experience gave me a genuine appreciation for the details
          connecting a design to a working part: tolerances, inspection,
          manufacturability, and clear instructions. A model on a screen
          becomes much more interesting when you have to figure out how
          someone will actually make and measure it on the shop floor.
        </p>

        <p>
          I also worked as a research intern in Hofstra’s ideaHUb makerspace,
          supporting prototyping, mechanical testing, troubleshooting,
          and equipment guides. Other projects have included a low-cost
          below-knee prosthetic leg and modifications that make children’s
          toys more accessible to users with limited mobility.
        </p>

        <h2>Linux, hardware, and open technology.</h2>

        <p>
          My interest in technology extends well beyond engineering software.
          I use Fedora Linux on my personal computer and enjoy exploring
          the desktop ecosystem, open-source applications, and the details
          that make a system feel good to use.
        </p>

        <p>
          That often turns into experimenting with software, troubleshooting
          hardware, comparing alternatives, or trying to understand why
          something behaves the way it does. I’m interested in performance,
          usability, repairability, and how much control a tool gives
          the person using it.
        </p>

        <h2>Learning to build with code and AI.</h2>

        <p>
          I use Python and MATLAB as engineering tools, and I build hobby
          software projects to explore ideas, modify software, and build small tools.
          Getting code to run is a starting point; understanding its assumptions,
          checking its mathematical behavior, and deciding whether the result is
          useful are the real work.
        </p>

        <h2>What you’ll find here.</h2>

        <p>
          This site is my technical notebook and independent engineering publication:
          a place for aerospace studies, project write-ups, simulation experiments,
          Linux explorations, and analysis of hardware and software.
        </p>

        <p>
          Some posts will work through an engineering question in detail with
          interactive equations and plots. Others will examine a new tool, compare
          approaches, or document something I tried in the machine shop.
        </p>

        <h2>Let’s connect.</h2>

        <p>
          If you’re working on something interesting in aerospace,
          engineering, or open technology, I’d be happy to hear from you.
        </p>

        <div class="about-contact-links">
          {site.email && (
            <a class="contact-card" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>
              <span class="contact-label">EMAIL</span>
              <span class="contact-val">{site.email} <ArrowIcon /></span>
            </a>
          )}
          {site.github && (
            <a class="contact-card" href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              <span class="contact-label">GITHUB</span>
              <span class="contact-val">@GlitchSlayed <ArrowIcon /></span>
            </a>
          )}
          {site.linkedin && (
            <a class="contact-card" href={site.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              <span class="contact-label">LINKEDIN</span>
              <span class="contact-val">Vansh Datta <ArrowIcon /></span>
            </a>
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sticky Technical Dossier Sidebar -->
      <aside class="profile-panel">
        <div class="dossier-badge">
          <Rocket />
          <span>TECHNICAL DOSSIER // DATA SHEET</span>
        </div>

        <div class="dossier-section">
          <span class="dossier-heading">ACADEMIC &amp; AFFILIATION</span>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">INSTITUTION</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">Hofstra University</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">DEGREE</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">BS Mechanical Engineering</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">CONCENTRATION</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">Aerospace Engineering ('27)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">LEADERSHIP</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">Co-President, AIAA Student Branch</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="dossier-section">
          <span class="dossier-heading">INDUSTRY &amp; SHOP EXPERIENCE</span>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">CO-OP</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">Arkwin Industries (6 mo.)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">DOMAINS</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">Hydraulic Actuators, CNC Tooling</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">RESEARCH</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">ideaHUb Makerspace Intern</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="dossier-section">
          <span class="dossier-heading">COMPUTING &amp; TOOLING</span>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">DAILY OS</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">Fedora Linux (Workstation)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">SIMULATION</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">Python (NumPy/SciPy), MATLAB</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dossier-item">
            <span class="dossier-key">CAD &amp; CAM</span>
            <span class="dossier-val">SolidWorks, GD&amp;T, Inspection</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="dossier-section">
          <span class="dossier-heading">ACTIVE PURSUITS</span>
          <ul class="dossier-list">
            <li>Blended-wing body subsonic aerodynamics</li>
            <li>Low-speed wind tunnel force instrumentation</li>
            <li>Aerospace actuation workholding fixtures</li>
            <li>Local-first Linux tools &amp; utilities</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="profile-bottom">
          <span class="status-dot"></span>
          <span>LAB STATUS: OPERATIONAL · ITERATING</span>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 36px;
  }

  .about-prose {
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .about-lead {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 22px);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--foreground);
    margin: 16px 0 28px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .about-contact-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .contact-card {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: all 0.16s ease;
  }

  .contact-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--surface-2);
  }

  .contact-label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.8px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .contact-val {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--foreground);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  /* Sticky Technical Dossier Panel */
  .profile-panel {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 24px;
    position: sticky;
    top: 90px;
  }

  .dossier-badge {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding-bottom: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 9.5px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .dossier-section {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    padding-bottom: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--border);
  }

  .dossier-section:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: none;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .dossier-heading {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 8.5px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    color: var(--subtle);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .dossier-item {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
  }

  .dossier-key {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 9.5px;
  }

  .dossier-val {
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .dossier-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .dossier-list li {
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .profile-bottom {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 9px;
    letter-spacing: 0.8px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .profile-panel {
      position: static;
      margin-top: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>
